Description: Synchronize avformat consumer start and stop
 The encoding thread now sets "running" itself once it is ready to
 encode, and consumer_start() waits for it: start returns only after
 the thread is running, or after it has failed and been joined, in
 which case start returns an error. A failed pthread_create() is
 reported the same way.
 .
 consumer_start() and consumer_stop() are serialized by a mutex, so
 stop cannot run while a start is in progress. A stop called from the
 consumer thread itself, for example by a consumer-fatal-error
 listener, only clears "running": it cannot join itself, and the start
 that may be waiting on that thread would otherwise deadlock. The next
 stop from another thread joins it. Previously such a stop tried to
 join itself, failed with EDEADLK and cleared "thread", so the caller's
 later stop joined nothing and close freed the consumer while the
 thread was still running (heap-use-after-free under ASan and TSan).
 .
 Builds on the previous commit, which moved the "running" write ahead
 of pthread_create() to fix #1333; the thread now owns that write.
 .
